A||N||3||RoadRocket||Steering Problem||||5||
Z||000000||RoadRocket||08-19-2001||01:38 PM||||OK, my Fiero's getting in better and better shape, but recently the wheel feels like its got a bit of drift in it. I can hold a straight line, but it feels like I'm a little drunk. Something wrong with the steering, obviously, but does anyone have any ideas as to exactly what it might be?<P><P>------------------<BR>Ed Dana<BR>88 Coupe.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||08-19-2001||02:36 PM||||Get a good 4-wheel alignment.<BR>If the alignment is off it will handle funny or drift/waddle. Also low air pressure in the tires can cause it too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||RoadRocket||08-20-2001||09:58 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>Get a good 4-wheel alignment.<BR>If the alignment is off it will handle funny or drift/waddle. Also low air pressure in the tires can cause it too.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks, but that has already been done, along with brand spanking new tires.<P>The problem is, I appear to have to problems, a little bit of drift and a little bit of oversteering. I replaced the suspension in an effort to correct the problem, it reduced it, but it didn't go away.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||2birds||08-20-2001||10:28 PM||||I assume your tires are all the same speed rating and tread pattern.  I had S-rated on the back with H-rated on the front, and it wanted to swap ends on me any time I touched the brakes. <BR>Also, the alignment shop should warranty the alignment, usually for at least 6 months or so.  Take it back to them and see what isn't right now.  <BR>The first time I had mine aligned after putting in the Moog slotted upper ball joints, the shop didn't tighten the bolts to lock them in place to the A-arm.  It's a real PITA to do, since the wheel has to come off each time to adjust them, and a lot of shops want extra cash to do it.||||reg||1
